WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.910
(November, the 46th of Shinka Era
 Shinjuku)

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.480
Our lips come together and tingle.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.040
We take our small glasses.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:20.160
Drink them up, hold each other close,
 and dance till we're spent.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:25.420
The promise that man made,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.540
I actually believed it.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.620
No chairs?

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.430
You eat them walking around.
 Everybody does it in the U.S.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.950
I don't care anymore, let it all end.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.290
It wasn't him, either.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.040
Where is it?

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.750
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.970
This world that you couldn't forgive
 is such a beautiful place

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:19.080
Are you saying everything that
 bears sadness is evil?

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.410
Even if the children crumble
 with guns of reality pointed at them

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.580
I am me and nothing else

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.620
I gain through gunpoint

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.750
Ready to fight

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.500
I'll rise like the break of dawn

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.070
I save them for the final day

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.330
Dream of the world
 for me and "fantasia"

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.000
It's time to go
 Unshaken wind

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.660
Change the world

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.040
I shake off my wavering gaze

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.000
And find my beloved justice

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:07.450
I live for the tomorrow
 that is unspoken of

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.160
Amidst evanescence and pain

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.730
Only the break of day drives me on

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.900
Until the day
 everything has returned

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.000
I face such horror tonight

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.000
The victims were all aliens
 from different planets.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.500
Aliens, huh.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.250
What was that defense force called?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.250
The EDC.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.250
That's it. I'm lousy with acronyms.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.640
Anyway, the agreement prohibits
 aliens from acting like humans, right?

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.520
But it did it anyway...
 An evil superhuman?

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.870
But there's also the Washizu case.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.020
You can't just kill them.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.620
Who are the suspects?

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.410
Raito Shiba.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.660
His random vandalism led
 to a dismantling order.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.200
But he resisted and is on the run.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.660
Extensive fugitive warrant number 693.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.080
Oh my. A lot has changed for him
 in such a short time.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.920
There's one more suspect.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.670
Jiro Hitoyoshi.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.160
He was part of the destruction
 3 years ago at Shinjuku.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.050
It's suspected that he has assisted
 several superhuman crimes.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.370
No fixed address.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.040
Do you mean it, Fuurouta?

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.540
He's the most suspicious.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:30.540
But it seems the perpetrator
 is someone else.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.160
Oh, a girl?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.660
A female superhuman?

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.910
Jiro Senpai might be behind her.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.620
He's unrelated this time.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.370
But he's soft towards women.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.370
Why would you know?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.750
The woman might be searching for
 a specific alien.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.870
If so, this will continue.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.410
This person...

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.580
I've seen her...

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.790
You called for me. Don't make me wait.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.480
Hikaru Misumi?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.450
Oh, Mr. Judas?

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:18.230
He stopped superhuman activities
 after that clash with Earth-chan.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:23.450
Rumors say this is
 an illegal hospital for superhumans.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:24.910
And Judas is there.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.240
But he was trying so hard
 to be a righteous superhuman.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.620
Things change after 4 whole years.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.700
You're closing the hospital?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.870
I'll start it up again soon.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.790
I want you to keep a patient for me.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.080
Why me?

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:41.450
We've met before.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.130
You know...

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.160
Angel Stars?

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.160
The patient is one of them.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.080
You sided with the U.S. Army,

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.910
but with students at Shinjuku.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.160
You just care about popularity.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.540
- No...
 - Forget about us.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.660
But save Aki.
 She's wanted for the alien murders.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.870
By your old colleagues.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.540
The alien murders, huh.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.250
Stop this madness.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.830
You'd never understand me.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.040
Your intentions are...

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.700
Health and Welfare Ministry
 Super Population...

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.370
Superhuman Bureau. We're arresting
 the serial alien killer.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.700
Meteortail!

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.370
- Jiro.
 - Jiro-san!

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.580
Let's go.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.350
Jiro-san, don't be fooled! She's...

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.450
An alien killer, wanted by the Bureau.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.940
So I'm protecting her.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.080
Hoshinoko, that's the princess carry.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.570
It's your dream...

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.250
Stop!

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.410
We won't let you!

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:06.800
You'll have to eat premade food.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.080
I don't care.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.950
What's this?

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.450
Rainbow Knight?

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.750
You're young but you know him?

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:19.830
I used to adore him as a child.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.910
It's perfect for fetching water.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:26.370
I hated how my big brother
 always played Rainbow Knight.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.160
I'd secretly wear a cape in my room.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:32.160
- That's real, you know.
 - Impossible.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.410
Forgot?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.620
It was to be displayed
 at last year's Expo.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.790
(December, the 44th of Shinka Era
 Osaka Expo under construction)

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.550
Welcome.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:54.160
The Mitsuya Superhuman Pavilion,
 built by the Mitsuya Conglomerate,

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.560
exhibits Japan's
 superhumans and future.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:01.310
There are only a handful
 of true superhumans now.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.790
But all humankind
 will become superhumans,

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:07.820
creating a bright future for Japan.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.450
This is a Japan 50 years from now.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.950
Jump on the "Travator"
 moving sidewalk to...

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.700
The 21st century!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.660
Don't move.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.080
Sir Mitsuya, remember me?

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:33.040
The Secret Functional Law
 has been shelved thanks to you.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.580
Superhumans won't be
 recognized in society.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:39.410
So why are you promoting superhumans?

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.620
Nowadays, superhumans
 are criminals in hiding

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.500
or the authority arresting them.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.120
Is this for atonement? No.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.620
You plan to wipe out all superhumans
 that don't comply with the government.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.330
Hence this promotion.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:09.040
This is the former Bureau ace
 we worked to create?

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.500
What a sorry sight.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:13.370
Akita, make up your mind.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.830
Akita?

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.370
Chief?

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.700
What's going on, Chief?

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:26.900
If you were in Sir Mitsuya's body,
 then what happened last year...

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.910
Councilor Mitsuya wanted to
 establish by law,

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.580
that there are humans and non-humans.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:35.780
To control them.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.830
But it's the truth.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.700
There are non-humans on this planet.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:45.290
You're the newspaper CEO and
 the Health and Welfare Ministry guy.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.830
We are from a world
 much more advanced than humans'.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:54.180
So we are responsible for leading
 you inferior beings.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.680
Space beings called Fumers.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.830
You know them, no?

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:02.830
I can't remember.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.500
Enemies of Teito Advertisement.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:09.940
They pressured Councilor Mitsuya
 to not revise the law...

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.370
So those Fumers...

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.450
Hey, what's wrong?

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.450
We can't be responsible
 for people we've fired.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.330
So you admit she's from Angel Stars.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.250
The one called Arachne.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.950
She's a former member.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.620
Why was she fired?

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.160
Same old story.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.450
Tell us.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:35.620
A scandal.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:36.720
Scandal?

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.200
Oh dear.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.580
Still too young to understand?

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.200
I do understand. It's...

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:46.730
Being with a man and...

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.230
Not necessarily.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.450
You are?

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.320
The name is Satomi.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.070
I'm the corporate advisor,
 but just by name.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.410
Yoshiaki Satomi, yes?

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.750
I've heard from Prof. Hitoyoshi.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.660
He's an acquaintance
 of Prof. Hitoyoshi?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:11.370
We will finish off Aki Haruka's case.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.450
Finish off...?
 You mean secure her, right?

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:15.970
Then we'll join...

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.910
I don't associate
 with Yokai and demons.

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:26.870
I don't team with former superhumans
 who conspired with the army, either.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.410
For our company,
 superhumans are products.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.500
Righteous beings that
 humans think of as ideal.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.870
Stain that image, and I won't put
 a superhuman price tag on them.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.120
Price tag?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:45.080
What's with that man?
 Treating us like the enemy.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.620
Public Security wants
 superhumans for weapons.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.870
The Bureau wants to
 protect superhumans.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.790
Teito wants to profit off superhumans.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.870
Humans sure are a pain.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:59.870
And Jiro wants to destroy the Bureau.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.080
Aren't you mad, Miss Emi?

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.000
Of course. And so I'll resort to this.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.440
Why'd you wait till now?

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.940
It's a shame for
 a woman to chase a man.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.330
Grossed out?

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.790
So Judas does modifications too?

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:38.250
I asked him to.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.700
To become stronger.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.200
A superhuman singer wasn't enough?

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.640
I was just doing as I was told to.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.910
Supporting students
 if they're popular,

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:50.410
and prosecuting them right after.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:51.450
But...

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:55.200
I understand.
 You got the urge to do right.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.620
You realized your own sense of justice
 instead of just obeying Teito.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.200
Justice this, justice that. Stop it.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:08.910
Are you stupid?
 That nonsense is so lame.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.000
Lame? That's just an
 excuse to not get serious.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:20.790
Our parents fought a war
 for the justice of this country.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:22.410
And they lost.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.200
It was because it didn't exist.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:29.200
They all fought believing
 they are justice.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.500
All that is over with.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:34.400
Jiro Hitoyoshi. You're out of date.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.200
Then you...

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.330
What's your name?

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:41.160
Aki Haruka.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.150
Haruka?

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.870
Aki Haruka, like autumn and spring.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:47.790
My name can't decide on a season.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.910
I guess I got tired of indecisiveness.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.670
I knew I'd seen her before.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.120
She's one of the Angel Stars.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:01.910
"Drummer Fanny dead.
 Cause of death undisclosed."

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.000
She was so young.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:05.680
The way it's written,
 could be suicide.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.160
I get it now.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:10.700
Fanny and I were dating.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.160
But you're a girl band.

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.950
The company called it a scandal.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:21.040
They said we weren't even
 fit to be superhumans.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:25.160
We had to fight because
 we were superhumans.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:30.620
But I got sick of being bound to
 somebody else's justice.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.250
So what happened to Fanny?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.790
I want to be free.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.750
Free?

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.330
Can't superhumans want freedom?

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.450
I don't get it.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.580
I don't have any justice in me.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.700
So... Fumer, was it?

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:57.140
That alien knows an absolute justice
 that humans don't understand, right?

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:59.150
Bring it here.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.790
Fumers don't exist anymore.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:04.030
Akita, stop!

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.330
Akita!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.410
We are incomplete beings.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.500
We must coexist with another being.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.160
Yes, and we can't last long
 with some average being.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:27.830
That's why we worked hard to create
 the perfect superhuman to carry us.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:30.090
That's what this pavilion was for.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:32.870
You don't have time for this talk.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.330
You cannot last without a body.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:39.950
That's right.
 This body is easiest to get.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:48.370
Your body's next.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.330
Why not just enter me directly?

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.910
We can only take over lifeless bodies.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:03.540
So you killed humans
 to take their bodies...

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:09.370
You protected superhumans
 and nurtured them.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:12.200
To take over their bodies.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.830
It's like farm-raising.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:17.180
Akita, stop talking and help.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:23.200
Is that what you made
 the Superhuman Bureau for?

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.690
Lock one!

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:34.700
That's the power that we desire.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.370
Lock two.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.790
That's why we...

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.410
Jiro.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.870
Chief.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:09.700
You made it so I'd unlock myself.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:13.330
I'll go wild like a beast now.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.950
But it'll also be the end of you.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.700
I grew to like you guys.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.000
Superhumans and humans.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.330
So I came to think that
 we should leave this planet.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:30.410
So you made me defeat your allies.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.660
And now, I'm going to enter you.

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.160
I'm still alive.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.850
You can't take me.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.580
That's why I'm going to die in you.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:46.730
I'll use my remaining strength
 to control the beast inside you.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:50.290
You can do that?

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:52.740
You just don't know how.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:59.250
Just like how the humans of this
 planet don't know their potential.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.330
The Fumers aren't here anymore. So...

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:16.120
So that's where they were.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.510
Inside you!

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:21.910
I don't care anymore,
 let it all end.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:24.870
I am disappearing.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:31.040
The phantom kiss is the last scene
 of the late show.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:35.660
Listen! I knew you were
 killing aliens to find Fumers.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:41.500
Fumers look for new hosts
 when their superhuman host dies.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.580
That's what you were after.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.370
She became a star.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.370
Your girlfriend?

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.950
We're the Angel Stars.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.540
She became a star of angels.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.200
That's why I have to go out to space.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:58.970
That's why you want Fumers' powers?

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:03.160
We're superhumans,
 but we're bound by chains.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:07.230
We just want to be free.
 Completely free!

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.150
Free...

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:14.500
I want to go to the Andromeda star
 like Master Ultima.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.160
He's a Fumer and human's child, right?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.410
Yeah, but...

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.040
Give me the Fumers.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:24.620
That higher intelligence that can
 move freely among stars!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:29.000
If a god really exists...

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.960
Take me away from here.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.290
Equus!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.370
Fumers are gone.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:41.140
He gave me his life.

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:44.040
You haven't seen my powers yet!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.290
What's that?

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:58.450
She's Aki Haruka, isn't she?

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.500
She was a giant-type superhuman?

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:03.450
She tested Jiro's secret.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.410
Let's go, Equus.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:32.060
He's fine in that state?

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.290
Come on, she's a girl!

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:57.080
Which side are you on?

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.300
So are you going to
 arrest her or Hitoyoshi?

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:02.830
Arrest, huh?

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:08.040
Thanks for leading us.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.750
Don't you not hang with freaks?

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.250
That's why I brought
 a true superhuman.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:19.830
Emi, Kikko!

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:22.040
Who does he think he is?

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.580
He called me Kikko.

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:28.200
Aki!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.660
Go.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:35.290
I'm not giving up.
 I'm going to space to be free.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:39.580
I'm a hero of justice
 but I can't always do right.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:42.330
A friend asked me once.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:44.580
I can't decide yet.

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:48.850
But if I stop thinking,
 I'll become him.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.500
Take it.

00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:59.230
It's all I can give you.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:03.330
Why let the criminal go?

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.160
And that's the real mask, right?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:07.500
Then Rainbow Knight's secret...

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.250
There's nothing. It's empty.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.620
What's this? It's empty.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.120
Was this a fake too?

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:19.370
No, it's real.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:20.540
Chief.

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.870
My consciousness will perish,
 so let me tell you.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:29.760
The greatest secret that
 Prof. Hitoyoshi and I had kept.

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:35.250
Rainbow Knight supposedly had
 secret powers in his mask and suit.

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:38.040
But he was just a regular human.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:44.580
A regular human could do all that
 just by hiding behind a mask.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:49.410
But a regular human wasn't enough
 for the establishment of the Bureau.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.790
We needed a superhuman
 to commit a crime.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:57.040
Then how are humans
 and superhumans different?

00:21:57.660 --> 00:22:01.750
That's why I came to
 want to trust you all.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:05.250
Tell me. What is a superhuman?

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:07.930
Rainbow Knight was human?

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:10.790
He pretended to be a superhuman?

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.930
That's not it.
 He really was a superhuman.

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:40.950
In this age where
 ideals are just a fantasy

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:47.950
Where are you going to
 reach out to?

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:50.790
Alone by yourself

00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:52.700
Always

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:54.620
Always

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:57.370
With somebody's justice

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:05.860
You're suffering to protect what?

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:10.120
If you're still captured...

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:11.950
I can't hold you

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.950
On these streets without any signs...

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:19.910
A child is crying

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:25.950
Ideals are just a toy, anyway

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:34.790
But you still reach out your hands

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:42.200
Righteous heroes are probably
 just beyond your reach

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:48.370
I don't mind
 I just want to keep watching...

00:23:49.660 --> 00:23:52.500
Just that one person

00:23:57.040 --> 00:23:58.790
Fly the skies, pierce the heavens.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:02.500
I'll win the gold
 even if I modify my body.

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:06.120
Even if I anger the gods,
 I'll jump bearing our flag.

00:24:06.450 --> 00:24:08.290
We are the Three Bird Men.

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:10.790
The nation's wings. A fake dream.
